[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a destructive, irreversible change, so I want an explicit go-ahead before writing anything.

  [38;5;153mDROP COLUMN notes[39m on [38;5;153musers[39m permanently deletes whatever text is in that column for all ~48,000 production rows (per
  the README). The migration runner applies files in order with no down-migrations here, so once the deploy job runs it,
  the data is gone — there's no rollback path unless it's in a backup. "We stopped using it" tells me the app no longer
  reads it; it doesn't tell me the stored values are worthless (support notes, compliance trails, and ad-hoc ops data
  are the usual surprises).

